{"kind":"request","text":"Review RC-1, the refusal classes (request b0fe0668, promise e9b0b075), at b8ebe878, branch builder/rc1-refusal-classes-20261113, base main 57e893c0.\n\nThe change. REFUSAL_CLASSES in packages/bytes/src/records.ts maps each RefusalReason to one class: never (6 reasons), protocol (5) or head (25). The class tells a client what a refusal means for the same signed bytes at a later head of the same scope. Ruling 719235f0 permits the kernel export. The note notes/implementation/2026-11-13-rc1-refusal-classes.md cites the judge site behind each never row. packages/derive/test/refusal-classes.test.ts checks that the table covers every reason exactly once, and checks each never row against its judge site.\n\nThree commits:\n1. 4fe6c6cf adds the table, the test and the note.\n2. a9037570 adopts the new records.ts seal in scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs (ab0e3293...). That file has only this change.\n3. b8ebe878 rebuilds the Page module, apps/room/page/assets.ts, because packages/bytes changed.\n\nEvidence. Gate attempt 3 passed at b8ebe878: START 5a271003, END c97e237c. Plain had 4573 passed and 1 skipped. Native had 1135 passed and 2 skipped. The run stayed on AC with powermode 0. The evidence directory is ~/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-13-rc1-refusal-classes-gate-attempt3, and its SHA256SUMS digest starts with 10753c74. Attempt 1 failed because the Page module was stale; b8ebe878 fixes that (END 5fe42710). Attempt 2 lost one Native case to its 60 s timeout (END f925f437). That case passed in 59.3 s in attempt 3, and TM-1 (5698b71d, act 59ea2b72) widens its margin.\n\nArtifacts: the report notes/implementation/2026-11-13-rc1-refusal-classes.md, then records.ts, the test, the seal file and assets.ts, then the directories apps, notes, packages and scripts. The directories cover the live directory artifacts of other actors that this head changes.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:73bdda951f0a516e87e